<div class="privacy-document">
  <section>
    <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p><strong>App:</strong> Number Path: Math Adventure</p>
    <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> August 29, 2026</p>
    <p>Number Path is an offline mathematical game. This policy explains what information the app handles when you use it.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>Number Path does not require an account. The app does not include its own advertising, analytics, crash-reporting, or online account service, and it does not collect or share personal information through its own services.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. Information Stored on Your Device</h2>
    <p>The app stores game progress, best times, and settings such as sound, haptics, and theme locally on your device.</p>
    <p>This local information is not uploaded by Number Path.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. External Apps and Links</h2>
    <p>If you choose <strong>Share</strong>, Android opens the system share sheet with a static invitation message.</p>
    <p>If you open the privacy policy or Play Store link, Android opens an external app. The selected external service may process information under its own privacy policy; Number Path does not receive that service data.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>4. Children and Personal Information</h2>
    <p>Number Path does not ask players to create an account or enter personal information.</p>
    <p>Do not include personal information in messages shared through another app.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>5. Data Deletion</h2>
    <p>Use <strong>Settings &gt; Reset progress</strong> to remove the locally stored game progress and best times.</p>
    <p>You can also clear the app storage or uninstall the app through Android settings.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>6. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>If the app data practices change, this policy will be updated with a new effective date before or when those changes take effect.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>7. Contact</h2>
    <p>For privacy questions, contact the developer using the contact details shown on the Number Path Google Play listing.</p>
  </section>
</div>

